3. PROPOSED WORKING SCOPE

Onboarding:
  - Google button immediately opens Home without authentication or Drive access.
  - Preserve the existing removal of Excel.
  - Keep Custom Database disabled.
  - Keep the blank Google logo placeholder as previously requested.

Home:
  - Calculate sales totals, transaction count, and stock warnings from local data.
  - Display recent transactions from the same records used by History.
  - Use a bounded, independently scrollable recent-transactions area.

Sell:
  - Display products with search and contextual product filters.
  - Cart, adding sale items, payments, and checkout remain unavailable.
  - Selling functionality is explicitly outside this phase.

Inventory:
  - Display local products.
  - Search by product name or SKU.
  - Filter by stock status, vendor, or category.
  - Proposed supporting functionality: basic product add/edit and product details.

History:
  - Display stored demo transactions.
  - Search by receipt number and apply date filters.
  - Proposed supporting functionality: read-only transaction details.

Tools:
  - Open Sync Status and Settings.
  - Identify unfinished tools clearly.
  - Vendors and Reports remain pending.
  - Recommended pending item: Stock Counts, until its workflow is defined.

Sync Status:
  - Show the offline state and pending local changes.
  - Sync Now must not report a successful upload while no cloud adapter exists.
  - Avoid presenting a fictional successful sync time as a real event.

Settings:
  - Disconnect the demo session and return to onboarding.
  - Reset local data through explicit confirmation.
  - Define and document whether reset clears records or restores demo fixtures
    before implementing the action.

Demo data:
  - Use unique receipt identifiers and consistent totals.
  - Home and History must read the same records.
  - Separate sample records from claims about actual external synchronization.

