These recommendations require the user's implementation decision; they have
not been implemented as part of this review.

5. LAYOUT AND STYLING REQUIREMENTS

  - Keep title bars, search fields, and filter controls fixed outside scrolling
    content.
  - Isolate product, transaction, and form content in their own scroll containers.
  - Give lists enough bottom padding to clear FABs, navigation, and system insets.
  - FABs must include icons.
  - Subpages must use chevron-left navigation.
  - Replace suitable Figma icons with Material icons.
  - Give every page and subpage its own Kotlin file.
  - Preserve relative positioning and responsive behavior even where Figma does
    not use auto layout.
  - Match the reference at 412 x 917 and reflow for other portrait sizes and
    larger system text.

